-- title:
--   Base change of a regular fibre over a perfect field
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by a single element $\varpi$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi)$, and assume the residue field of $A$ is perfect. Let $\mathcal O$ be a Noetherian commutative local $A$-algebra which is essentially of finite type over $A$, and suppose the image of $\varpi$ in $\mathcal O$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Assume moreover that the quotient $\mathcal O/(\varpi\mathcal O)$, by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$, is a regular local ring, and that its Krull dimension satisfies $\dim \mathcal O/(\varpi \mathcal O) \le 1$. Let $k$ be a field equipped with an $A$-algebra structure for which $\varpi$ maps to $0$. Finally let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime ideal of $\mathcal O \otimes_A k$ whose contraction along the ring homomorphism $\mathcal O \to \mathcal O \otimes_A k$, $x \mapsto x \otimes 1$, is exactly $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. The conclusion is that the localisation $(\mathcal O \otimes_A k)_{\mathfrak q}$ is an integral domain.
--
--   This is a form of geometric regularity over a perfect field: a fibre that is regular of dimension at most one over a perfect residue field remains locally a domain after an arbitrary field extension of the base, the proof passing through formal smoothness and regularity of the localisations of a standard smooth algebra over a field. It is used in the analysis of the irreducible components of a fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1$, where local integrality of the base-changed fibre is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isDomain_localization_atPrime_tensorProduct_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_perfectField.lean

